# Replace with a real Postgres URL — the template hostname "host" will fail with getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@YOUR-DB-HOST/dbname?sslmode=require
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here
# Supabase: IPv4 is preferred by default for *.supabase.co (fixes getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND for logged-in sessions). Set PG_USE_IPV4=0 to disable.
# If TLS to Postgres fails with "self-signed certificate in certificate chain" (corporate proxy / inspection), set PG_SSL_ALLOW_UNSAFE=1 for local dev only. Omit in production if not needed.
# PG_USE_IPV4=0
# PG_SSL_ALLOW_UNSAFE=1
# Signs session cookies. MUST be set to a real random value — an unset var falls
# back to a literal published in this repo, which makes every session forgeable.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
SESSION_SECRET=change-me
# LOCAL DEV ONLY. Accepts any 6-digit OTP, for use until an SMS provider is
# wired (otp.ts §sendOtpSms). Only honoured when NODE_ENV=development as well.
# Never set this in a deployed environment — phone is the primary credential.
OTP_DEV_BYPASS=1

# TESTING — makes every login code this exact value, instead of a random one.
# The code is still hashed, still expires, still locks out after 5 wrong
# guesses; only the randomness is gone. Narrower than OTP_DEV_BYPASS, which
# accepts anything, and unlike it this IS honoured in production builds — the
# deployed staging build runs with NODE_ENV=production and is what it is for.
#
# ANYONE WHO KNOWS A PHONE NUMBER CAN LOG IN AS ITS OWNER WHILE THIS IS SET.
# Unset it before this environment has real customers. Must be exactly 6
# digits or it is ignored.
OTP_FIXED_CODE=
# Optional — enables Redis session store and postal lookup cache
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
ITD_COMPANY_ID=
ITD_EMAIL=
ITD_PASSWORD=
ITD_CUSTOMER_CODE=
ITD_API_COMPANY_ID=
ITD_COOKIE=
# Powers the AI support agent, and the vision fallback that reads a GST
# certificate uploaded as a photograph rather than the portal PDF
# (server/gstCertificate.ts). Unset is supported: a text-layer PDF still reads
# for free, and a photo comes back unverified instead, which blocks the account
# until they upload the real certificate.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Absolute base URL of this server — used to construct KYC document file_path URLs for ITD
PUBLIC_URL=https://your-app.railway.app
# BOMBINO_UPI_VPA / BOMBINO_UPI_NAME were removed along with the doorstep QR.
# Nothing reads them. Delete them from any deployed environment too — a VPA
# sitting in config that no code serves is a trap for the next person.
# ── Razorpay (A4, pay-now at booking) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys. Test keys start rzp_test_.
# Unset is a supported state: the pay-now endpoints return 503 and the other
# three payment methods keep working, so a deploy without keys still books.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# A SEPARATE secret, set when you create the webhook — not the API secret.
# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks → add {PUBLIC_URL}/api/payments/razorpay/webhook
# subscribed to payment.captured, payment.failed, refund.processed and
# refund.failed. Without this the webhook rejects every delivery, and a
# customer whose browser dies mid-payment is left unpaid on our side.
# The two refund events are how a dashboard-issued refund reaches the order —
# we never issue refunds from the app, only record them.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# ── TEMPORARY: pay-now test bypass ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to let a signed-in customer settle their OWN pay-now order without
# the gateway, from a switch that then appears next to Pay Now. It writes a
# real payments row (tagged source: "test_mode", reference test_<order id>) and
# marks the order paid — so an order can be marked PAID WITH NO MONEY MOVING.
#
# For testing the flows behind a paid order while the Razorpay account is
# unusable. Unlike OTP_DEV_BYPASS this is honoured in production builds too,
# because the client tests on a deployed staging environment — which means the
# variable is the only thing protecting real payments. Unset it before this
# environment takes any. The server prints a boxed warning at boot while it is
# on, and logs every settle.
#
# Delete this, server/paymentsTestMode.ts, POST /api/payments/test/settle,
# client/src/lib/paymentsTestMode.ts and PaymentTestModeSwitch.tsx when the
# gateway works.
PAYMENTS_TEST_MODE=

# ── WhatsApp (Tata Tele Omni BSP) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Omni panel > Settings > Channels > WhatsApp. The token identifies the WABA,
# so there is no sender number to configure.
#
# Unset is a supported state: every send is skipped and logged, in-app
# notifications are unaffected, and the login OTP falls back to the server
# console. Nothing breaks — the customer simply hears nothing.
#
# EVERY MESSAGE IS A PRE-APPROVED TEMPLATE. See docs/whatsapp-templates.md for
# the catalogue that has to exist in the Omni panel before any of this sends.
TATA_WA_TOKEN=
# Defaults to https://wb.omni.tatatelebusiness.com when unset.
TATA_WA_BASE_URL=
# The last path segment of the webhook URL registered in the Omni panel:
#   {PUBLIC_URL}/api/whatsapp/webhook/{TATA_WA_WEBHOOK_SECRET}
# It is the entire authentication on that endpoint, so treat it as a password.
# Carries delivery receipts (sent/delivered/read/failed) and the STOP word.
TATA_WA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# 1 = render and log messages, write the whatsapp_messages row, send nothing.
# Defaults ON in development, so a click-through against the shared Supabase
# project cannot message whoever is seeded in it. Set to 0 to send for real.
WA_DRY_RUN=1
# Bearer secret for POST /api/internal/wa/agent-schedule, the endpoint an
# external scheduler calls for the agent digest (?kind=digest) and the
# before-the-window reminders (?kind=reminders). Unset = the endpoint 404s.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
WA_CRON_SECRET=

# ── SMS (fallback for the login code) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Used only when WhatsApp cannot deliver an OTP — most often a dual-SIM
# customer whose WhatsApp lives on their other number. Phone is the only
# credential in this app, so without this that person cannot log in at all.
#
# NO VENDOR IS WIRED YET. See the VENDOR GAP in server/sms.ts. Unset is a
# supported state: the WhatsApp path works normally and only the fallback is
# missing, logged loudly each time it is needed.
#
# Indian transactional SMS also needs TRAI DLT registration before anything
# sends: Bombino registered as a Principal Entity, a 6-character sender ID,
# and the OTP template registered SEPARATELY from the WhatsApp one. An
# unregistered template is dropped by the operator with no receipt.
SMS_API_KEY=
# The DLT-approved 6-character sender ID, e.g. BMBNOX.
SMS_SENDER_ID=


# Cashfree VRS — identity verification and Smart OCR. One set of credentials
# and one balance covers both halves of onboarding:
#
#   server/cashfreeIdentity.ts  proves the Aadhaar, PAN and GST *numbers*
#                               before anything is uploaded. Aadhaar comes from
#                               the customer's own DigiLocker under their
#                               consent (they never type it); PAN is checked
#                               against the name the Income Tax Department
#                               holds; GSTIN against the GST portal.
#   server/cashfreeOcr.ts       reads the number off the *document* uploaded
#                               afterwards and refuses it if it disagrees.
#   server/gstCertificate.ts    does the same for the GST certificate, which
#                               Cashfree Smart OCR has no document type for --
#                               the PDF text layer, then an OpenAI vision call
#                               for a photograph. See OPENAI_API_KEY.
#
# Sandbox keys are `cfsk_ma_test_*`.
# REQUIRED for signup: an account cannot be created unless every identity
# number is verified AND every identity document came back verified, so with
# these unset nobody can register. See scripts/check-cashfree-identity.ts and
# scripts/check-cashfree-ocr.ts.
#
# BOTH PRODUCTS MUST BE PROVISIONED ON THE CASHFREE ACCOUNT. They are enabled
# per account, and an un-provisioned one answers 200 with "<product> is not
# enabled for this account" rather than a 4xx. Offline Aadhaar Verification is
# not enabled on ours, which is why Aadhaar goes through DigiLocker instead —
# confirm DigiLocker itself is enabled before relying on it.
CASHFREE_VRS_CLIENT_ID=
CASHFREE_VRS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# sandbox | production  (default: sandbox)
CASHFREE_VRS_ENV=sandbox
# Pinned API version; only change deliberately (default: 2024-12-01)
# CASHFREE_VRS_API_VERSION=2024-12-01

# ── TEMPORARY: identity-verification bypass ─────────────────────────────────
# Accept an identity number WITHOUT checking it with any authority. Per check,
# because the two are not equally available:
#
#   IDENTITY_BYPASS=aadhaar        skip the DigiLocker journey only
#   IDENTITY_BYPASS=pan            skip the PAN lookup only
#   IDENTITY_BYPASS=gstin          skip the GST portal lookup AND the
#                                  certificate check (with no verified GSTIN
#                                  there is nothing to match the file against)
#   IDENTITY_BYPASS=aadhaar,pan    skip those two
#   IDENTITY_BYPASS=1              skip all three (older spelling, still honoured)
#
# Leave it UNSET first and try the real path. Set `aadhaar` only if DigiLocker
# turns out not to be provisioned on the account — the boot log and the server
# log both name that case explicitly ("DigiLocker is not enabled on this
# Cashfree account"). Do NOT bypass pan or gstin: both work today, against real
# numbers, and switching them off would give up the checks that work.
#
# With aadhaar bypassed there is no consent journey to run, so the form falls
# back to a plain 12-digit field and POST /api/signup/identity/aadhaar/bypass
# banks whatever is typed. That endpoint 404s unless this flag names aadhaar.
#
# A bypassed number is recorded as status = 'bypassed' in identity_verifications
# rather than 'verified', so ops can find every account that opened on an
# unchecked number, and the customer is told on screen that it was not checked.
#
# ANY 12 DIGITS / ANY 10 CHARACTERS ARE ACCEPTED FOR A BYPASSED CHECK. Like
# PAYMENTS_TEST_MODE this is honoured in production builds too, because staging
# runs NODE_ENV=production. Unset it before this environment has real
# customers. The server prints a boxed warning at boot naming exactly which
# checks are off, and logs every number it lets through.
#
# Needs migrations/add_identity_verifications.sql applied either way — the
# table holds the bypassed rows too.
IDENTITY_BYPASS=
